versized images and implement compression recommendations</p></div></div></div><div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-50 to-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6 md:p-8"><div class="mb-6"><div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-question-mark w-5 h-5 text-[#00AEEF]" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3"></path><path d="M12 17h.01"></path></svg><h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-black">Questions Fréquemment Posées</h3></div><p class="text-sm md:text-base text-gray-600">Questions courantes sur cet outil et comment l'utiliser efficacement</p></div><div class="bg-white rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-4 md:p-6"><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">1</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">Why does image compression matter for SEO?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Image compression directly impacts page load speed, which is a core ranking factor for Google. Faster-loading pages improve user experience, reduce bounce rates, and increase time on site-all signals that boost SEO performance. Google's Core Web Vitals (LCP, CLS, FID) heavily penalize slow image loading.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">2</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">What&#x27;s the difference between WebP, JPEG, and PNG formats?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>JPEG is best for photos with lossy compression. PNG uses lossless compression ideal for graphics with transparency. WebP is a modern format offering 25-35% smaller file sizes than JPEG and 60-80% smaller than PNG with similar quality. WebP supports both lossy and lossless compression plus transparency, making it the best choice for most web images.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">3</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">How do I balance image quality with file size?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Use 80-85% quality for JPEG and WebP-the human eye can barely detect the difference from 100%, but file sizes are 3-5x smaller. For hero images, you can go up to 90%. Always compress before uploading, and use tools like TinyPNG, Squoosh, or ImageOptim to find the optimal balance.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">4</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">What is lazy loading and should I use it?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Yes, absolutely. CDNs like Cloudflare, Cloudinary, or imgix serve images from geographically distributed servers closer to your users, reducing latency. Many CDNs also offer automatic format conversion (serving WebP to supported browsers), responsive image generation, and on-the-fly compression, saving you hours of manual optimization.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">5</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">Should I use a CDN for images?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">6</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">What size should I make responsive images?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Never serve a 4000px image for a 400px container. Use the srcset attribute to provide multiple sizes (e.g., 400w, 800w, 1200w, 1600w) and let browsers choose the optimal version. Resize images to their maximum display dimensions-for example, if your hero image displays at 1920px max, don't upload a 4000px version.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">7</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">What are the best free image compression tools?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Top tools include TinyPNG (batch PNG/JPEG compression), Squoosh (WebP conversion with quality preview), ImageOptim (Mac app for lossless compression), and Sharp (Node.js library for automation). For bulk processing, consider Cloudinary's free tier or build automation with Sharp in your build pipeline.</p></div></div></div><div class="mt-6 text-center" ><p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-2">Vous avez encore des questions ?</p><a href="/contact" class="text-[#00AEEF] font-semibold hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm md:text-base">Contactez notre équipe pour obtenir de l'aide<svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3"></path></svg></a></div></div></div></section><section class="py-16 bg-white border-t border-gray-100"><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4"><div class="text-center mb-10"><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-black mb-3" style="f